  17: | NHANES post | fixed 0.10 | 0.448 | 0.890 | 0.361 | 0.921 |
  18: 
  19: ## Table S4. Triage-oriented high-sensitivity operating points
  20: 
  21: A screening/triage tool is typically tuned to high sensitivity. At sensitivity fixed to 0.85 and 0.90, the table gives the resulting specificity, positive predictive value (PPV), negative predictive value (NPV), the share of the population flagged (flag rate), and the number needed to screen to identify one case (NNS = 1/PPV). At these fixed-sensitivity operating points the 8-item deployment model performs comparably to the full 17-predictor model, even though its post-pandemic *discrimination* is 0.016 AUROC lower (§3.6).
  22: 
  23: | Model | Set | Target | Specificity | PPV | NPV | Flag rate | NNS |
  24: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
  25: | 17-predictor | Internal | sens 0.85 | 0.616 | 0.076 | 0.991 | 0.400 | 13.1 |
  26: | 17-predictor | Internal | sens 0.90 | 0.505 | 0.064 | 0.993 | 0.509 | 15.7 |
  27: | 17-predictor | NHANES pre | sens 0.85 | 0.524 | 0.142 | 0.974 | 0.507 | 7.1 |
  28: | 17-predictor | NHANES pre | sens 0.90 | 0.394 | 0.121 | 0.977 | 0.631 | 8.3 |
  29: | 17-predictor | NHANES post | sens 0.85 | 0.486 | 0.187 | 0.959 | 0.555 | 5.4 |
  30: | 17-predictor | NHANES post | sens 0.90 | 0.385 | 0.169 | 0.965 | 0.649 | 5.9 |
