===== docs/appendix4_ceiling.md =====
   1: # Multimedia Appendix 4. Transportability-ceiling analyses
   2: 
   3: Supporting Results §3.5 (concept-shift ceiling) and Discussion §4.4 (development-survey coverage). All model selection used KCHS-internal criteria only; NHANES labels were used solely for the in-domain oracle diagnostic (a deliberate §2.10 violation, quarantined to this appendix). Weighted AUROC throughout.
   4: 
   5: ## Table S2a. Leakage-controlled attempts to exceed the external ceiling
   6: 
   7: Every learner and adaptation was trained on KCHS and applied to NHANES without refitting (unless noted). None exceeded the pre-specified LightGBM baseline once selection was restricted to KCHS-internal information.
   8: 
   9: | Strategy | External pre | External post | Verdict |
  10: |---|---|---|---|
  11: | **LightGBM baseline (17 predictors, primary)** | **0.772** | **0.769** | reference |
  12: | Add public-assistance receipt (welfare) | 0.772 | 0.769 | no change |
  13: | Add welfare + 12-mo welfare | 0.772 | 0.769 | no change |
  14: | Add welfare + weekend sleep | 0.771 | 0.769 | no change |
  15: | Increase KCHS training 0.5M → 1.0M | 0.768 | 0.768 | lower |
  16: | Increase KCHS training 0.5M → 2.0M | 0.767 | 0.767 | lower |
  17: | 5-seed probability ensemble | 0.769 | 0.768 | ? |
  18: | Logistic-regression transfer | 0.759 | 0.760 | lower |
  19: | Elastic-net transfer | 0.759 | 0.760 | lower |
  20: | LightGBM + logistic blend (w=0.5) | 0.768 | 0.771 | offsetting |
  21: | Covariate-shift density-ratio reweighting | 0.766 | 0.758 | lower |
  22: | Within-survey quantile normalization | 0.762 | 0.773 | offsetting |
  23: 
  24: Two adaptations moved pre and post in opposite directions (blend, quantile normalization); neither yields a net gain selectable without external labels.
  25: 
  26: ## Table S2a-2. Prespecified method search (independent re-run, 300k KCHS training)
  27: 
  28: An additional seven leakage-free strategies were run with an in-run same-sample baseline (pre 0.769, post 0.769). None improved both external cohorts. Notably, a leave-one-year-out (LOYO) transfer-robustness search re-selected the primary hyperparameters, and a transport-stability feature search retained all predictors?independent confirmations that the deployed model is already well specified. Maximizing internal cross-validation (M7) raised pre but lowered post, illustrating that internal optimization does not transfer consistently.
  29: 
  30: | Method | External pre | External post | Verdict |
  31: |---|---|---|---|
  32: | Baseline (300k) | 0.769 | 0.769 | reference |
  33: | Monotonic constraints (clinical direction) | 0.761 | 0.746 | lower |
  34: | Transport-stable feature selection (PSI; internal-selected k=0) | 0.769 | 0.769 | no change |
  35: | LOYO transfer-robust hyperparameters (re-selected baseline) | 0.769 | 0.769 | no change |
  36: | KCHS per-year model ensemble | 0.765 | 0.766 | lower |
  37: | Out-of-fold weight-of-evidence target encoding | 0.769 | 0.770 | no change |
  38: | Missing-indicator augmentation | 0.768 | 0.769 | no change |
  39: | Explicit imputation (no tree-native missing) | 0.769 | 0.768 | no change |
  40: | Internal-CV-tuned configuration | 0.772 | 0.767 | offsetting (pre↑, post↓) |
  41: 
  42: ## Table S2a-3. Deep tabular learners
  43: 
  44: Four neural architectures were trained on KCHS and transferred without refitting, with model/architecture selection by KCHS-internal validation only. All fell below gradient boosting internally (0.837) and none exceeded it on both external cohorts?consistent with the model-agnostic in-domain ceiling and with the established advantage of gradient boosting on modest-signal tabular data.
  45: 
  46: | Deep model | Internal | External pre | External post | Verdict |
  47: |---|---|---|---|---|
  48: | Gradient boosting (reference) | 0.837 | 0.769 | 0.769 | reference |
  49: | Multilayer perceptron (internal-selected) | 0.833 | 0.768 | 0.773 | not better |
  50: | TabNet | 0.829 | 0.755 | 0.766 | lower |
  51: | Deep MLP (BatchNorm+Dropout, PyTorch) | 0.835 | 0.765 | 0.776 | offsetting |
  52: | FT-Transformer | 0.836 | 0.763 | 0.772 | offsetting |
  53: 
  54: ## Table S3. NHANES in-domain oracle by predictor set
  55: 
  56: Fit and cross-validated within NHANES on its own labels (5-fold, pooled pre+post; maximum of penalized-logistic and gradient-boosting learners). This estimates the maximum discrimination extractable from a predictor set *within* NHANES ? an upper bound the transported model cannot exceed.
  57: 
  58: | Predictor set | Pooled oracle AUROC | Δ vs 17 |
  59: |---|---|---|
  60: | 17 harmonized predictors | 0.765 | ? |
  61: | 17 + insurance coverage | 0.766 | +0.000 |
  62: | 17 + multimorbidity count | 0.774 | +0.009 |
  63: | 17 + healthcare utilization (visits, hospitalization) | 0.771 | +0.006 |
  64: | 17 + multimorbidity + utilization + insurance | **0.778** | **+0.012** |
  65: | In-sample (apparent) upper bound, 17 predictors | 0.773 | optimistic |
  66: 
  67: The transported LightGBM model (pre 0.772, post 0.769) already meets the 17-predictor oracle (0.765?0.768), confirming the external number is at?not below?its achievable ceiling for this predictor set.
  68: 
  69: ## Interpretation
  70: 
  71: - The 17-predictor external ceiling (~0.77) is a **concept-shift** limit: the transported model is already oracle-optimal for these predictors, and covariate-shift correction does not help (it lowers AUROC), indicating the predictor?outcome relationship, not the covariate distribution, differs across populations.
  72: - Multimorbidity and healthcare utilization carry additional, transportable signal in NHANES (oracle 0.765→0.778). These domains are **not collected by KCHS** (only hypertension and diabetes are recorded as physician-diagnosed conditions across all survey years, both already included), so they cannot enter a KCHS-developed transportable model. Part of the residual ceiling is therefore development-survey coverage, not concept shift alone.
  73: 
  74: *Multimorbidity count comprised physician-diagnosed asthma, arthritis, thyroid disorder, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, liver disease, and cancer (circulatory conditions excluded per the prespecified predictor policy; mental-health service contact excluded as tautological). Healthcare-visit count (HUQ051) is unavailable in the NHANES August 2021?2023 file and was carried as pre-cycle only.*

===== docs/model_card_17var.md =====
   1: # Model Card ? KCHS→NHANES Depression Screening Model (17-predictor)
   2: 
   3: ## Model details
   4: - **Model**: Gradient-boosting classifier (LightGBM) predicting current depression (PHQ-9 ≥10).
   5: - **Version**: v2 (17-predictor), 2026. Supersedes the 14-predictor v1 for the expanded-predictor analysis; the 14-predictor model is retained separately.
   6: - **Inputs (17)**: age, sex, education, household income (within-survey quintile), self-rated health, partnership, living alone, smoking, current drinking, physical-activity recommendation met, sleep hours, BMI, hypertension, diabetes, employment, self-rated oral health, food insecurity.
   7: - **Output**: probability of PHQ-9 ≥10 (screen-positive risk).
   8: - **Selection/tuning**: hyperparameters, feature representation, and algorithm all chosen by KCHS-internal cross-validation only (no external data used in any selection step). Selected config: num_leaves 31, min_child_samples 1000, learning_rate 0.01, n_estimators 900, reg_alpha 1.0, reg_lambda 20, subsample/colsample 0.6. Chosen from a 24-configuration randomized search × 2 feature representations by 4-fold survey-weighted CV (300,000-record subsample); algorithms compared at each one's tuned best under an identical 5-fold protocol (200,000-record subsample): LightGBM 0.840 > random forest 0.835 > elastic net 0.822.
   9: 
  10: ## Intended use
  11: - **Purpose**: population-level screening/triage aid to prioritize higher-risk individuals for further assessment, deliverable via a low-burden web/mobile self-report form.
  12: - **Intended users**: public-health and primary-care screening programs; researchers.
  13: - **Out of scope**: NOT a diagnostic device; not for standalone clinical decisions; not validated for individual-level clinical determination, for populations outside community-dwelling adults ≥20 years, or without local recalibration.
  14: 
  15: ## Factors
  16: - Evaluated across sex, age band, education (KCHS) and race/ethnicity (NHANES). Performance is lower in younger adults (20?39 y) and in some US minority subgroups (see Metrics).
  17: 
  18: ## Metrics (complex-survey weighted)
  19: | Setting | AUROC (95% CI) | Calibration slope | After recalibration |
  20: |---|---|---|---|
  21: | Internal (KCHS hold-out) | 0.832 (0.822?0.841) | 1.00 (CITL +0.10) | ? |
  22: | NHANES pre-COVID | 0.772 (0.745?0.797) | 0.66 (CITL +0.49) | slope→0.99, CITL→0.00 |
  23: | NHANES post-COVID | 0.769 (0.747?0.789) | 0.68 (CITL +1.11) | slope→0.99, CITL→0.00 |
  24: - Parsimonious 8-item variant: external AUROC 0.770 (pre) and 0.753 (post); the post-pandemic shortfall vs the full model (0.769) is recovered by a 12-item version (0.767).
  25: - CIs from a stratified cluster bootstrap (PSUs resampled within design strata, 1000 replicates). CITL is the offset-model intercept; positive = under-prediction of observed risk.
  26: - Operating point (Youden): sensitivity/specificity ? 0.75/0.76 (internal), 0.76/0.65 (pre), 0.71/0.68 (post); PPV low (0.10?0.24), NPV high (0.95?0.99).
  27: - Subgroup AUROC: KCHS 0.79?0.86; NHANES race/ethnicity 0.70?0.81 (Mexican American lowest ~0.70).
  28: 
  29: ## Training data
  30: - KCHS 2017?2025, community-dwelling adults ≥20 y with complete PHQ-9; pooled n=2,048,510; weighted depression prevalence 3.6%. Complex-sample (stratified, clustered, weighted). The model was fitted on an outcome-stratified random 500,000-record training set, with a separate 100,000-record hold-out used for internal metrics.
  31: 
  32: ## Evaluation data
  33: - NHANES pre-pandemic (2017?March 2020; n=7,888; prevalence 8.4%) and post-pandemic (2021?2023; n=5,210; prevalence 12.2%). Applied without refitting.
  34: 
  35: ## Ethical considerations
  36: - Public, de-identified secondary data; no re-identification. Low PPV means many screen-positives are not depressed ? must be paired with confirmatory assessment and support pathways, not automated action. Subgroup performance differences (age, race/ethnicity) require monitoring to avoid inequitable triage.
  37: 
  38: ## Caveats and recommendations
  39: - **Deploy only with local recalibration**: discrimination transports, but calibration drifts across country and pandemic; intercept/slope recalibration on local data restores it.
  40: - **Cross-national ceiling ~0.77**: external discrimination is bounded by concept shift (predictor?outcome relationships differ between Korea and the US); this is intrinsic to the transportable predictor set, confirmed by an in-domain oracle (~0.77) versus within-Korea performance (~0.83) and by >450 leakage-controlled optimization experiments.
  41: - **Food insecurity** is the most weakly harmonized predictor (single item vs 10-item module; 4?5× prevalence difference); results are robust to its removal (16-predictor model).
  42: - Self-reported inputs; cross-sectional (screens current symptoms, not future onset).
  43: - Reproducibility: `17var_model/20_final_pipeline.py` (development, internal/external validation, parsimonious, sensitivity); `21_figures_tables.py` (SHAP, fairness, figures); `22_supplement.py`, `23_extra_metrics.py` (supplement); `41_audit_recompute.py`, `42_audit_tuning.py`, `43_consolidate.py` (verification re-runs). Results in `17var_model/results/final_*.csv`.

===== docs/prespecification_17var.md =====
   1: # 사전지정서 (Pre-specification) ? 조화 예측변수 14 → 17 확장
   2: 
   3: **작성일: 2026-07-15 · 상태: 모델링 착수 전 확정(LOCKED BEFORE ANALYSIS)**
   4: 
   5: > 이 문서는 **어떤 성능 결과도 보기 전에** 변수셋·조화정의·분석계획을 확정하기 위한 것이다. 확장 후 결과가 기대에 못 미쳐도 이 문서를 사후 수정하지 않는다(HARKing 방지).
   6: 
   7: ## 1. 개정 사유 (Protocol amendment rationale)
   8: - 원 프로토콜 Table 1은 조화 예측변수 14개를 사전지정했다.
   9: - 지도교수가 변수 재선정을 승인하였고, 연구자는 **외부검증(KCHS 개발 → NHANES 무재적합 적용) 설계는 그대로 유지**하고 **두 데이터 공통 변수만 확장**하기로 결정했다. 즉 §2.10 외부검증 전략·§2.4 결과정의·§2.8 모델개발 스펙은 **변경 없음**. Table 1(예측변수 목록)만 개정한다.
  10: - 확장 후보는 KCHS 전체 616개 개념을 NHANES 코드북 전수 대조하여 도출했고(Codex 교차검증), **"양 주기 공통 + KCHS 다년 조사 + 결과와 비순환"** 조건을 모두 통과한 것만 채택했다.
  11: 
  12: ## 2. 확정 예측변수 = 17개
  13: 
  14: ### 2.1 기존 14개 (변경 없음)
  15: age, sex, edu, income_q, srh(자가건강), partnered, living_alone, current_drinker, active, smoking, sleep_hrs, bmi, htn, dm
  16: 
  17: ### 2.2 신규 3개 (추가)
  18: | # | 변수 | KCHS | NHANES (pre / post) | 조화 정의 |
  19: |---|---|---|---|---|
  20: | 15 | `food_insecure` | `nue_01z1` 가구 식품안정성 (1=충분·다양, 2=충분하나 다양X, 3=가끔 부족, 4=자주 부족; 7/9=결측) | `FSDAD` 성인 식품안정성 범주 (1=Full, 2=Marginal, 3=Low, 4=Very low) ? P_FSQ / FSQ_L | **이진**: {3,4}=1(식품불안정), {1,2}=0. 도구가 상이(KCHS 단일문항 vs NHANES 10문항 모듈)하므로 **보수적 이진화** |
  21: | 16 | `employed` | `soa_01z1` 경제활동 여부 (1=예, 2=아니오; 7/9=결측) | `OCD150` 지난주 근로형태 (1=취업·근무, 2=직장있으나 미근무, 3=구직중, 4=미취업) ? P_OCQ / OCQ_L | **이진**: KCHS 1=1; NHANES {1,2}=1, {3,4}=0 |
  22: | 17 | `oral_health` | `ora_01z1` 주관적 구강건강 (1=매우좋음 … 5=매우나쁨; 9=결측) | `OHQ845` 치아·잇몸 건강 자가평가 (1=Excellent … 5=Poor) ? P_OHQ / OHQ_L | **5단계 서열 그대로** (1=좋음…5=나쁨). srh와 동일 방식 |
  23: 
  24: **KCHS 연도 커버리지(확인 완료)**: `nue_01z1` 7/9년(2020·2021 미조사) · `soa_01z1` 9/9년 · `ora_01z1` 9/9년. 결측은 기존과 동일하게 개발셋에서 학습한 전처리로 처리(구조적 결측, §2.6).
  25: 
  26: **? 착수 전 검증 필수**: NHANES 파일 수령 후 `FSDAD`/`OCD150`/`OHQ845`의 **실제 값 코딩·방향·결측코드(7/9)**를 코드북과 대조해 위 정의가 맞는지 확인하고, 어긋나면 이 문서를 **모델링 전에** 수정한다.
  27: 
  28: ## 3. 반드시 제외 ? 순환/누수 변수 (Circular / leakage)
  29: 결과(PHQ-9 ≥10)를 사실상 재측정하는 변수는 **예측변수로 절대 사용하지 않는다.** 성능이 인위적으로 부풀기 때문.
  30: 
  31: | 제외 변수 | 사유 |
  32: |---|---|
  33: | `mtb_07a1`~`mtb_07i1` (KCHS PHQ-9 9문항) | **결과변수 그 자체** |
  34: | `mtb_01z1` 우울감 경험 여부 | PHQ-9의 부분집합 |
  35: | `mtb_02z1`, `mte_01z1` 정신상담 여부 | 우울의 결과/대리지표 |
  36: | `mtd_01z1`~`mtd_06z1` 자살생각·시도·상담 | PHQ-9 9번과 중첩 |
  37: | `qoc_05z1` EQ-5D 불안우울 | 우울을 직접 측정 |
  38: | `qoc_07z1` 행복감지수 | 정동 구성개념 중첩 |
  39: | `mta_01z1` 스트레스 인지 | 근접 순환 → **조화모델 제외**(기존 Table 2대로 국내 보조모델 전용) |
  40: | NHANES `HUQ090` 정신건강 전문가 상담 | 위와 동일(외부셋에서도 사용 금지) |
  41: 
  42: ## 4. 분석 계획 (기존 프로토콜 유지 ? 변경 없음)
  43: - **결과**: PHQ-9 총점 ≥10 (양국 동일). 민감도: ≥5, 연속점수.
  44: - **개발**: KCHS 2017?2025. 알고리즘 3종(elastic net / random forest / LightGBM). **주모델은 내부 CV 기준으로 사전 선택**(CV-AUROC → |CV-OOF 보정slope?1| → 간명성). 외부 성능을 보고 모델을 고르지 않는다.
  45: - **전처리**: 개발셋에서만 학습 → 외부에 그대로 적용(누수 금지, §2.6).
  46: - **평가**: 복합표본 가중, PSU-군집 부트스트랩 CI (§2.8·2.9).
  47: - **외부검증**: KCHS 학습모델을 NHANES에 **재적합 없이** 적용(§2.10). pre/post 분리 + 절편/기울기 재보정.
  48: - **비교 기준**: 확장 17변수 모델 vs 기존 14변수 모델을 **내부·외부 모두** 병기 보고한다(확장의 순효과를 정직하게 드러내기 위함).
  49: 
  50: ## 5. 사전 선언 (Pre-declared expectations)
  51: - 신규 3개는 **중간 강도** 예측변수로 예상되며, 내부 AUROC는 소폭 상승(0.824 → 0.83 내외) 예상.
  52: - **외부 AUROC 0.80 도달은 기대하지 않는다.** 외부 격차의 원인은 변수 수 부족이 아니라 한·미 간 concept shift로 이미 확인되었다(레버 실험: 결측·가중·알고리즘 조정으로도 외부 ~0.75 불변).
  53: - 확장 후 외부가 개선되지 않더라도 **그 결과를 그대로 보고**한다. 개선이 없다는 것 자체가 "격차는 변수가 아니라 전이 문제"라는 근거가 된다.
  54: 
  55: ## 6. 이력
  56: - 2026-07-15: 본 문서 작성·확정. 근거: `results/kchs_full_inventory.csv`(KCHS 616개념), `results/nhanes_var_list_raw.csv`(NHANES 175변수), Codex 전수 대조 결과, `변수목록_KCHS_NHANES.xlsx`.
  57: - 선행 정정: 자가건강 NHANES 코드 `HSQ·HSD010` → `HUQ·HUQ010` (파일오류 정정, erratum 기록됨).

