docs/appendix4_ceiling.md:66:The transported LightGBM model (pre 0.772, post 0.769) already meets the 17-predictor oracle, confirming the external number is at—not below—its achievable ceiling for this predictor set.
docs/appendix4_ceiling.md:81:- The 17-predictor external ceiling (~0.77) is a **concept-shift** limit: the transported model is already oracle-optimal for these predictors, and covariate-shift correction does not help (it lowers AUROC), indicating the predictor–outcome relationship, not the covariate distribution, differs across populations.
docs/appendix4_ceiling.md:82:- Multimorbidity and healthcare utilization carry additional, transportable signal in NHANES (oracle 0.765→0.778). These domains are **not collected by KCHS** (only hypertension and diabetes are recorded as physician-diagnosed conditions across all survey years, both already included), so they cannot enter a KCHS-developed transportable model. Part of the residual ceiling is therefore development-survey coverage, not concept shift alone.
