  53: 
  54: **Interpretation.** Tuned to a triage-appropriate 85% sensitivity, the model flags roughly half of the external population (pre 51%, post 55%) at a PPV of 0.14?0.19, i.e., a number needed to screen of 5?7 in the US cohorts; the 8-item form is nearly identical (NNS 5.6?7.6). After local recalibration, net benefit is positive and exceeds both default strategies at threshold probabilities of 0.10?0.15 in every dataset, supporting use as a low-burden digital triage aid rather than a diagnostic test.
